    "question": "Ivan had $10 and spent 1/5 of it on cupcakes. He then spent some money on a milkshake and had only $3 left. How much is the milkshake?",
    "gold": "5",
    "answer": "Ivan spent a total of $10 - $3 = $<<10-3=7>>7 on cupcakes and a milkshake.\nThe cost of the cupcake is $10 x 1/5 = $<<10*1/5=2>>2.\nSo, $7 - $2 = $<<7-2=5>>5 was spent on the milkshake.\n#### 5"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much money Ivan spent on the milkshake, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate how much money Ivan spent on cupcakes.\n2. Determine how much money Ivan had after buying the cupcakes.\n3. Find out how much money Ivan spent on the milkshake.\n\nFirst, we calculate how much money Ivan spent on cupcakes. Ivan had $10 and spent \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) of it on cupcakes. So, the amount spent on cupcakes is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5} \\times 10 = 2\n\\]\nThis means Ivan spent $2 on cupcakes. After buying the cupcakes, the amount of money Ivan had left is:\n\\[\n10 - 2 = 8\n\\]\nNext, we know that after buying the milkshake, Ivan had $3 left. Therefore, the amount of money he spent on the milkshake is:\n\\[\n8 - 3 = 5\n\\]\nSo, the amount of money Ivan spent on the milkshake is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
